From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Home Assistant OS <homeassistant@home-assistant.io>
Date: Thu, 26 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rename chardev class and device nodes for coexistence

Rename the sysfs chardev class from "hailo_chardev" to "hailo8_chardev"
and the device node prefix from "hailo" to "hailo8", creating /dev/hailo8N
nodes and /sys/class/hailo8_chardev/.

This allows hailo_pci (Hailo-8) and hailo1x_pci (Hailo-10/15) to be
installed simultaneously on the same system without conflicting on the
shared class name or device node namespace.
---
 linux/pcie/src/pcie.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/linux/pcie/src/pcie.c b/linux/pcie/src/pcie.c
--- a/linux/pcie/src/pcie.c
+++ b/linux/pcie/src/pcie.c
@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@ static bool force_boot_linux_from_eemc = false;
 static bool support_soft_reset = true;

-#define DEVICE_NODE_NAME "hailo"
+#define DEVICE_NODE_NAME "hailo8"
 static int char_major = 0;
 static struct class *g_chrdev_class = NULL;

@@ -258,7 +258,7 @@ static int hailo_pcie_insert_board(struct hailo_pcie_board *pBoard)

     if (!g_chrdev_class) {
-        g_chrdev_class = class_create_compat("hailo_chardev");
+        g_chrdev_class = class_create_compat("hailo8_chardev");
         if (IS_ERR(g_chrdev_class)) {
